[17592186240745 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186238347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240745 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240745 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240745 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240745 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186238167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240745 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ece2ff83-0d7a-55e7-848c-06928bf3c946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20=0$ given that $x=3-\\text{i}$ is a solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0788e647-7a4e-5549-adea-a1cd056a2776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240891 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=3-\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}}=3+\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(3-\\text{i}+(3+\\text{i)})x+(3-\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+({3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-6x+10$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+2 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-6x+10\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-\\phantom{2}2x+20} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-12x+20 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-12x+20}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-6x+10)(x+2).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2,3\\pm \\text{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11x-116=0$ given that $x=-5+2\\text{i}$ is a solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1be54b7-7530-59ba-90a4-e2866a7b30e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240892 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11x-116.$\n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=-5+2\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{-5+2\\text{i}}=-5-2\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(-5+2\\text{i}))(x-(-5-2\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(-5+2\\text{i}))(x-(-5-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(-5+2\\text{i}+(-5-2\\text{i)})x+(-5+2\\text{i})(-5-2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+((-5)^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+29 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}+10x+29$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+10x+29\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,{x}^{3}+\\phantom{1}6{x}^{2}-11x-116} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}+29x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}+40x-116 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,{-4{x}^{2}+40x-116}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n        \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}+10x+29)(x-4).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=4,-5\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263934 #edb/ref 1080 "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263934 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263934 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c5e09aa-a71a-5bc1-abdb-ffbee8ae45ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264066 #edb/ref 1080 "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264066 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264066 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7b00896b-7411-5bea-b442-6e238235690f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264072 #edb/ref 1080 "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264072 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264072 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c1c69e8-11c6-5242-a605-cf735a7f46aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264286 #edb/ref 1080 "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "967a322b-3f8a-5022-9edc-92691060c3ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265080 #edb/ref 1080 "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265080 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265080 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee11f2f0-386f-5dd5-b7b7-a51ec3fc0b57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265080 