 17592186045417] [17592186299198 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299198 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299198 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186298392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299198 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a66018ec-422c-5e0e-b376-357aef68a84e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1069 "q-31871" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1071 "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${B}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5898f79-8d87-5e96-a0ad-da8516834a84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299700 #edb/ref 1074 "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $B$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${B}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1080 "x=B\\,d\\,A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6788781d-31d5-5bd7-b27b-68afaa4d9325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1080 "x=B\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9bded5b5-b83d-570e-9629-cd29113e20b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1080 "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4a497d7-ea8a-5a5f-b4fd-1d8c483ff5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1080 "x=BA\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b6d2cc68-86a2-5604-8401-931a07c9e6b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1080 "x=AB\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e304282a-e8e7-5d48-b8b7-fb2bbc3eab5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 175921860454