f the vector-valued function $f(t)=2{t}^{3}\\,i+(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401364 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c16eaa20-dd31-5858-a148-07284cbf2219" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401364 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $2{t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401365 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b2067c3d-0d1e-5094-9c41-cc29fa1d1f8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401366 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401366 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401366 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e8b48905-c922-5f0b-904d-031f2f366d2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401367 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi +2n\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401367 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401367 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07837613-c6cb-599f-a1fe-60f06f0661aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401368 #edb/ref 1080 "n\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401368 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401368 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "823a0eb9-049b-54c7-87a1-4762c639c714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401369 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5f740a3-7481-581f-876f-a404eea190e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401370 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401370 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401370 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "730966c2-9ffc-5f1d-9533-075afe811e99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1071 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-{t}^{3})\\,i+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7adf6f23-c582-5c46-b1a7-7edbfe6210af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401378 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-{t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401379 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9a56ee90-9fa8-5ebf-a7cd-271d63b533b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401380 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ede8e16-494c-5ead-ba64-5838ef07def5" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
